cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "langstate: compress long LLM conversations into visible, checkable working state"
abstract: "langstate is a small experimental Python library for OpenAI-format message lists. It keeps system messages and recent turns verbatim, summarizes older history into a visible [SCAFFOLD STATE] system message, and returns the same list-shaped interface that chat clients already accept. A validate function gives a deterministic receipt for the literal facts named explicitly. It is a functional prototype/library, not a lossless archive, a structured state store, or production infrastructure."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Bosch Rodriguez"
    given-names: "Rolando"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-4896-1112"
    affiliation: "Hermes Labs"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/hermes-labs-ai/langstate"
version: "0.2.1"
keywords:
  - "context compression"
  - "conversation state"
  - "LLM"
  - "message summarization"
  - "validation"
